---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Services"
  description="The 30-Day Operations Diagnostic, fixed-scope automation builds, and embedded engineering for organizations in Portland, Oregon and beyond"
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero-topo section bg-gradient-to-b from-dark-bg via-dark-surface to-dark-bg">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
        <h1 class="mb-6 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Services</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-text-secondary">
          Operations automation, data systems, and AI engineering. Fixed price, one engineer,
          production results. Field data services are on their <a href="/field-data/" class="link">own page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Diagnostic -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <div class="mb-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">The 30-Day Operations Diagnostic</h2>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-accent-green/20 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-accent-green">
            Available now
          </span>
        </div>
        <p class="mb-8 text-lg text-text-secondary">
          <strong class="text-text-primary">$12,000. Half at signing, half at delivery. Thirty days from kickoff.</strong>
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-accent-blue">1 · A process map of your five costliest manual workflows</h3>
            <p class="text-text-secondary">
              Who does what, how many hours a month it takes, where errors and delays enter, and
              what each one costs you. Built from interviews with the people who do the work, not
              from an org chart.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-accent-cyan">2 · One workflow automated and running in production</h3>
            <p class="text-text-secondary">
              Not a prototype. The one with the best ratio of pain to effort. It ships with an
              audit log, error handling, a runbook your team can follow, and a 30-minute training
              session.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-accent-green">3 · A 12-month roadmap</h3>
            <p class="text-text-secondary">
              What to automate next and in what order, what to build versus buy, what each item
              costs, and where AI genuinely helps versus where a spreadsheet is the right answer.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="mb-4 mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">How the 30 days run</h3>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm text-text-secondary">
            <thead class="text-text-primary">
              <tr class="border-b border-dark-border">
                <th class="py-2 pr-4">Week</th>
                <th class="py-2">What happens</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-dark-border"><td class="py-2 pr-4">1</td><td class="py-2">Kickoff. Interviews with 5–8 staff. Read-only access to the systems involved.</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-dark-border"><td class="py-2 pr-4">2</td><td class="py-2">Process map delivered. Together we pick the workflow to automate. Scope agreed in writing.</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-dark-border"><td class="py-2 pr-4">3</td><td class="py-2">Build, in your environment or ours, under your data-handling rules.</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">4</td><td class="py-2">Production cutover, runbook, training. Roadmap delivered. Closing session with leadership.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="mb-4 mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">What we need from you</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-text-secondary">
          <li>One sponsor who can make decisions inside 48 hours.</li>
          <li>Access to the people who do the work, about six hours of their time in total.</li>
          <li>Read access to the systems in scope. Write access only for the workflow we automate, scoped and revocable.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="mt-10">
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Book a 30-minute call</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Fixed-scope builds -->
  <section class="section bg-dark-surface">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <div class="mb-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">Fixed-Scope Builds</h2>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-accent-green/20 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-accent-green">
            Available now
          </span>
        </div>
        <p class="mb-6 text-lg text-text-secondary">
          <strong class="text-text-primary">$5,000–$15,000 per workflow, quoted after a call.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="text-text-secondary">
          For organizations that already know the process they want gone. Intake forms that file
          themselves. Reconciliation that names every mismatch. Reports that assemble from the
          source systems every morning. Documents that become records without re-keying. Each
          build ships with an audit log, a runbook, and training, and runs without us.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Embedded -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <div class="mb-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">Embedded Engineering</h2>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-accent-purple/20 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-accent-purple">
            From early 2027
          </span>
        </div>
        <p class="mb-6 text-lg text-text-secondary">
          <strong class="text-text-primary">$25,000–$35,000 per month. Six-month minimum. Roughly half-time presence.</strong>
        </p>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            An engineer inside your organization rather than a vendor outside it. In the first 90
            days, your worst manual process runs itself with an audit trail and a runbook. After
            that, one new workflow into production every 30 to 45 days.
          </p>
          <p>
            Scope in writing every 30 days. A one-page written report every week. A 45-minute
            steering session with leadership every month. Everything documented as it is built,
            so that if the engagement ended tomorrow your team could run what exists.
          </p>
          <p>
            Not staff augmentation, not an agency, not a black box. Your systems, your data, your
            repositories.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Data handling -->
  <section class="section bg-dark-surface">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">Data Handling</h2>
        <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-blue">In your environment</h3>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
              Code runs on your infrastructure. Nothing leaves.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-cyan">On ours</h3>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
              For sensitive data, processing runs on hardware we own and control, with no
              third-party model provider. Transcription, document extraction, and classification
              can all run this way.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-green">Hosted, under agreement</h3>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
              Where a hosted model is the right tool: a provider with a signed data-processing
              agreement, no training on your data, and configurable retention. Named in scope.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
          Named accounts only, credentials rotated to you at handover, working copies deleted at
          engagement end and confirmed in writing. We never train models on your data and never
          reuse anything from one client for another. Full data-handling sheet available on request.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-bold">Who Does the Work</h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
          Devin MacArthur. A data-systems engineer who has built the daily pipelines, CRM
          integrations, document-extraction tools, and internal platforms behind a
          41,000-member statewide organization, and who ships production systems with agentic
          AI tooling. One engineer, start to finish. No handoffs. <a href="/about/" class="link">More on the About page.</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="section bg-dark-surface">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-bold">Start With a Call</h2>
        <p class="mb-8 text-text-secondary">
          Thirty minutes. Tell us the process that eats the most time. If a spreadsheet would fix
          it, we will say so on the call.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Book a call</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
